    {
      "math_academy_id": "q-122673",
      "knowledge_point_id": "bf1a53c0-e652-5732-9d5a-5aad004c2676",
      "knowledge_point": "Solving Trigonometric Equations Using the Sin-Cos-Tan Identity Under a Modified Domain",
      "problem": "Given that ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are the solutions of the equation $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-6\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=0$ for $-{180}^{∘}<x\\le {180}^{∘}$ what is the numerical value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2},$ rounded to the nearest degree?",
      "worked_solution": "We divide both sides of the equation by $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ and use the identity $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}.$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-6\\operatorname{cos}⁡x & =0 \\\\ \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}-\\frac{6\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}-\\frac{6\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}}{\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}-6 & =0 \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡x-6 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we rearrange the equation and isolate $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-6 & =0 \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(6)≈{80.538}^{∘}\n$$\n\nSince ${80.538}^{∘}$ lies inside the given domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}={80.538}^{∘}.$\n\nTo find the other solution, we subtract ${180}^{∘}$ from the principal value. Hence,\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}={80.538}^{∘}-{180}^{∘}≈-{99.462}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nFinally, the numerical value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}$ is $80.538\\cdot (-99.462)≈-8\\,010.$",
