      "knowledge_point_id": "bf1a53c0-e652-5732-9d5a-5aad004c2676",
      "knowledge_point": "Solving Trigonometric Equations Using the Sin-Cos-Tan Identity Under a Modified Domain",
      "problem": "Given that ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are the solutions to the equation $4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-16\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=0$ for $-\\pi <x\\le \\pi ,$ what is the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2},$ rounded to $3$ decimal places?",
      "worked_solution": "We divide both sides of the equation by $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ and use the identity $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-16\\operatorname{cos}⁡x & =0 \\\\ \\frac{4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}-\\frac{16\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}-\\frac{16\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}}{\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}} & =0 \\\\ 4\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}-16 & =0 \\\\ 4\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-16 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we rearrange the equation and isolate $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4\\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =16 \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =\\frac{16}{4} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(4)=1.325\\,817\\,663…≈1.325\\,818\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $6$ decimal places. \n\nSince $1.325\\,818$ lies inside the given domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}=1.325\\,818.$\n\nTo find the other solution, we subtract $\\pi $ from the principal value. Hence,\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}=1.325\\,817\\,663…-\\pi =-1.815\\,774\\,989…≈-1.815\\,775\n$$\n\nrounded to $6$ decimal places.\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}≈1.325\\,818\\cdot (-1.815\\,775)≈-2.407\n$$\n\nrounded to three decimal places.",
