    {
      "math_academy_id": "q-330590",
      "knowledge_point_id": "bf1a53c0-e652-5732-9d5a-5aad004c2676",
      "knowledge_point": "Solving Trigonometric Equations Using the Sin-Cos-Tan Identity Under a Modified Domain",
      "problem": "In **ascending order**, rounded to two decimal places in radians, the solutions to the equation $2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=5\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,$ for $-\\pi \\le x<\\pi ,$ are\n\n${x}_{1}≈$\n{{field-1}}$,\\,{x}_{2}≈$\n{{field-2}}.",
      "worked_solution": "We divide both sides of the equation by $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ and use the identity $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & =5\\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\ \\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x} & =\\frac{5\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x} \\\\ 2\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x} & =5 \\\\ 2\\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =5 \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =\\frac{5}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{5}{2})≈1.190\\,29\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $5$ decimal places. \n\nTo find another solution in the interval $[-\\pi ,\\pi )$, we subtract $\\pi :$\n\n$$\nx≈1.190\\,29-\\pi ≈-1.951\\,30\n$$\n\nrounded to $5$ decimal places. \n\nSo, in ascending order, rounded to two decimal places, the solutions are \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}≈-1.95,\\,{x}_{2}≈1.19.\n$$",
